From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josef Holzmayr <jester@theyoctojester.info>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] env: Provide ENV_REDUNDANT alias for
 SYS_REDUNDAND_ENVIRONMENT

Version skew between two layers, not a board problem.

Upstream U-Boot renamed SYS_REDUNDAND_ENVIRONMENT to ENV_REDUNDANT
after v2025.04. oe-core wrynose ships u-boot 2026.01, which has the new
name, and meta-mender's include/config_mender.h is written against it:

  #ifndef CONFIG_ENV_REDUNDANT
  # error CONFIG_ENV_REDUNDANT is required for Mender to work.

meta-freescale pins u-boot-imx to NXP's lf_v2025.04 branch, which
predates the rename, so the build fails at do_compile even though
redundant environment support is correctly enabled under the old name.

Add ENV_REDUNDANT as a hidden symbol tracking SYS_REDUNDAND_ENVIRONMENT
rather than renaming, because the rest of this tree still refers to the
old name.

Drop this patch once u-boot-imx rebases past the rename.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [compatibility shim for a downstream tree]

Signed-off-by: Josef Holzmayr <jester@theyoctojester.info>
---
 env/Kconfig | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/env/Kconfig b/env/Kconfig
--- a/env/Kconfig
+++ b/env/Kconfig
@@ -474,6 +474,16 @@ config SYS_REDUNDAND_ENVIRONMENT
 	  which is used by env import/export commands which are independent of
 	  storing variables to redundant location on a non volatile device.
 
+config ENV_REDUNDANT
+	bool
+	default y if SYS_REDUNDAND_ENVIRONMENT
+	help
+	  Compatibility alias for SYS_REDUNDAND_ENVIRONMENT. Upstream U-Boot
+	  renamed the symbol after v2025.04; this tree still uses the old
+	  name. Provided so that code written against the new name, such as
+	  meta-mender's generated include/config_mender.h, sees a consistent
+	  value.
+
 config ENV_FAT_INTERFACE
 	string "Name of the block device for the environment"
 	depends on ENV_IS_IN_FAT
--
